WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:07.890
Yesterday, the Dow Jones Industrial Average
had once again a disastrous, disastrous day,

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:14.049
falling twelve point nine three percent in
a single trading day.

00:00:14.049 --> 00:00:18.060
That is just under 3000 points in one day.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:24.019
If we look at the worst declines in history
by points, yesterday was the worst day ever.

00:00:24.019 --> 00:00:28.419
Now, I know I said this two weeks ago and
I said it twice last week.

00:00:28.419 --> 00:00:29.619
It keeps happening.

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:35.830
And in fact, if you look at the biggest single
day point declines in history, nine of the

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:41.980
largest fifteen point declines in history
have come in the last few weeks.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:48.020
Now, if we look at declines by percentage,
which may be more valuable in some sense.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:54.690
Yesterday was the second worst stock market
decline by percentage ever at twelve point

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.910
ninety three percent.

00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:02.059
The only time that the stock market had a
worse day than yesterday on a percentage basis

00:01:02.059 --> 00:01:07.619
was the day known as Black Monday, October
19, 1987.

00:01:07.619 --> 00:01:09.570
A historically bad day.

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:15.049
That's the only day that was a worse day than
yesterday by percentage.

00:01:15.049 --> 00:01:21.509
And otherwise, you're looking at worse than
the 1920s Great Depression numbers, OK, not

00:01:21.509 --> 00:01:23.310
the 2008 Great Recession.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:30.320
Yesterday, stocks were down more by percentage
than during any day of the Great Depression

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:31.930
of the 1920s.

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:33.119
Think about that.

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:38.260
And this has now wiped out all of the gains
of the Trump stock market of the last thirty

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.260
eight months.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:43.350
When Donald Trump took office, the Dow was
just a few points under twenty thousand one

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:44.780
hundred.

00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.210
That's where we ended yesterday.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.460
Twenty thousand one eighty eight.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.259
We're back to where we were.

00:01:50.259 --> 00:01:53.510
All of the gains of the Trump administration
are gone.

00:01:53.510 --> 00:02:00.060
And unfortunately, this level of erratic stock
market performance and the declines are likely

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.100
not over.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.399
We could have a long way to go.

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:05.850
Entire industries are unfortunately going
to be decimated.

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.610
So the question is, what can we do?

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:10.300
The Fed printing money is having minimal impact.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.660
The usual suspects are going to get bailed
out, the airlines, the cruise ship companies

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.130
and many more.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:18.660
But what about individuals but about small
businesses?

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.690
There's going to be some capital injections,
money made available through small business

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:23.920
association loans.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:28.520
There will be some other stimulus, but there
will be businesses destroyed by this.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:33.380
I don't know how the countless restaurants
that are currently relegated to takeout and

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:35.950
delivery only survive this.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:40.120
Their landlords are going to want rent unless
rent is suspended or forgiven or made up by

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.250
the government.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.920
Many restaurant owners are going to say, I
just have to walk away.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.980
I have to walk away from the restaurant.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:52.710
Even with rent support given by state or federal
government, states or state or federal governments.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:55.610
Many restaurants are not going to survive
because they're just not going to make enough

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:56.610
money and enough money.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:02.910
So right away, we probably need a combination
of some kind of universal basic income for

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:08.820
people making under X amount or businesses
whose gross revenues are under Y amount.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:12.610
I don't know what those those numbers are,
but we probably need something like that.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.830
Mitt Romney has suggested a thousand a month.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:20.940
Ro Karna has a proposal that's a $6000 one
time payment for people making under 65k.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.410
We need something like that.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:29.540
Number two, we are going to need the government
to step in and say we will make or guarantee

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:32.010
